    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0375" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg263"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-03-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1069.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a letter from Count Komura, minister for foreign affairs, dated yesterday,
                    the 3d instant, in reply to my note to him of January 25 conveying to him the
                    nature of your telegram of the 20th of January on the subject of the Manchurian
                    railways. I have indirect information that the officials of the foreign office
                    believe in the sincerity of your purpose, and that this reply has been fully
                    considered and contains an expression of their genuine sentiments.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d233-a1.xml" xpointer="d233-a1"/>
